# Hostile Hostel // Creeping Inn, both faces in one game, because the back face is reached only by three activations.
# "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Put a soul counter on this land. Then if there are three or more soul counters on it,
# remove those counters, transform it, then untap it. Activate only as a sorcery": refused in Bot2's upkeep on turn 2 with
# Mox Sapphire and the Hostel untapped (CR 602.5d); on turn 5 paid from two lands with one mana left, and a Mountain can't
# be sacrificed for it; at two counters (turn 7) it stays a land, at three (turn 9) the counters come off, it transforms
# (CR 701.27a) and untaps. "{T}: Add {C}" on turn 3. The Inn has been under Bot1's control since turn 1, so it attacks at
# once (CR 302.6). "Whenever this creature attacks, you may exile a creature card from your graveyard. If you do, each
# opponent loses X life and you gain X life, where X is the number of creature cards exiled with this creature": a
# Lightning Bolt in Bot1's graveyard and Bot2's discarded Yargles can't be chosen; X is 1 on turn 9, nothing on turn 11
# (declined), 2 on turn 13, when two Ornithopters can't both be chosen. "{4}: This creature phases out" on turn 13 leaves one of five mana; it phases in on Bot1's
# untap step (CR 502.1) still remembering its two cards (the 2021-09-24 ruling), so X is 3 on turn 15.

